($bc38299$love-realtalk-05$bc38299$,$bc38300$small_gap_both_content$bc38300$,$bc38301$Case dismissed. Echoes matched.$bc38301$,$bc38302$$bc38302$,$bc38303$You both catch yourselves comparing at almost exactly the same rate, which means neither of you is more haunted by the past than the other, you're each hearing the same faint echo occasionally, nothing more. That matched rate means the comparisons, when they do happen, are just an old habit passing through, not a sign either of you is secretly stuck somewhere else.$bc38303$,$bc38304$name one time a comparison crossed your mind and you let it pass without guilt. same.$bc38304$,$bc38305$Case dismissed. Echoes matched.$bc38305$,$bc38306$Approved v4 template$bc38306$,$bc38307$Root Swap$bc38307$,$bc38308$$bc38308$,$bc38309$name one time a comparison crossed your mind and you let it pass without guilt.$bc38309$,$bc38310$same.$bc38310$,$bc38311$Both of you write down your actual comparison frequency, honestly, on the same note and seal it together as proof it's mutual and minor.$bc38311$,$bc38312$Case dismissed. Echoes matched.$bc38312$),
($bc38313$love-realtalk-05$bc38313$,$bc38314$small_gap_split$bc38314$,$bc38315$Case dismissed. Case, dropped.$bc38315$,$bc38316$[A] = the partner who indicated it bothers them.$bc38316$,$bc38317$Same rate of comparison, but [A]'s turned it into evidence of disloyalty, while [B] never read theirs that way at all. The frequency's identical, only one of you built a court case against yourself for it. Dropping that case means [A] gets to have an old, occasional thought cross their mind without treating it as proof of something being wrong.$bc38317$,$bc38318$name, out loud, that an occasional passing comparison doesn't mean disloyalty. reassure once, specifically, that it doesn't read as a betrayal to you.$bc38318$,$bc38319$Case dismissed. Case, dropped.$bc38319$,$bc38320$Approved v4 template$bc38320$,$bc38321$Rename$bc38321$,$bc38322$[A] = the partner who indicated it bothers them.$bc38322$,$bc38323$name, out loud, that an occasional passing comparison doesn't mean disloyalty.$bc38323$,$bc38324$reassure once, specifically, that it doesn't read as a betrayal to you.$bc38324$,$bc38325$Both of you write a joint statement, 'occasional old echoes don't mean anything real,' and save it for next time the guilt shows up.$bc38325$,$bc38326$Case dismissed. Case, dropped.$bc38326$),
($bc38327$love-realtalk-05$bc38327$,$bc38328$small_gap_both_discontent$bc38328$,$bc38329$Case dismissed. Ghost, named and managed.$bc38329$,$bc38330$$bc38330$,$bc38331$You're both haunted by the same faint, unnamed presence sometimes, and you're both a little uneasy about it, without realizing you're each carrying the exact same ghost quietly. Naming that shared ghost turns two private worries into one thing you can actually talk about, which tends to make old echoes fade faster than silence ever does.$bc38331$,$bc38332$name what actually helps you let the comparison go when it happens. same.$bc38332$,$bc38333$Case dismissed. Ghost, named and managed.$bc38333$,$bc38334$Approved v4 template$bc38334$,$bc38335$Reframe$bc38335$,$bc38336$$bc38336$,$bc38337$name what actually helps you let the comparison go when it happens.$bc38337$,$bc38338$same.$bc38338$,$bc38339$Both of you write down, together, one shared strategy for letting old echoes pass, title the note 'Our Ghost-Busting Plan,' and keep it.$bc38339$,$bc38340$Case dismissed. Ghost, named and managed.$bc38340$),
($bc38341$love-realtalk-05$bc38341$,$bc38342$large_gap_both_content$bc38342$,$bc38343$Case dismissed. Territory, being redrawn.$bc38343$,$bc38344$[A] = compares more; [B] = rarely does.$bc38344$,$bc38345$[A]'s occasional comparisons aren't a sign of one foot out the door, they're an old map still occasionally overlaying new territory, a navigation habit, not a destination. [B]'s clean slate isn't superior, it's just [B]'s old map genuinely faded faster, which happens differently for everyone. Between the two of you, that gap closes naturally with time, not effort.$bc38345$,$bc38346$name the comparison when it happens, lightly, instead of hiding it. respond with patience rather than alarm when it's named.$bc38346$,$bc38347$Case dismissed. Territory, being redrawn.$bc38347$,$bc38348$Approved v4 template$bc38348$,$bc38349$Shared Discovery$bc38349$,$bc38350$[A] = compares more; [B] = rarely does.$bc38350$,$bc38351$name the comparison when it happens, lightly, instead of hiding it.$bc38351$,$bc38352$respond with patience rather than alarm when it's named.$bc38352$,$bc38353$Both of you write down one thing about this relationship that's genuinely, specifically new territory, unlike anything before, and keep it, dated, as proof the map is updating.$bc38353$,$bc38354$Case dismissed. Territory, being redrawn.$bc38354$),
